+ $('#same_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:form {:class "form-inline form-inline-header"} [:select {:name "id", :id "other_games_select", :class "form-control"} [:option {:value ""} "In other Games"] "\n" [:option {:value "239"} "1932"] "\n" [:option {:value "267"} "1948"] "\n" [:option {:value "281"} "1952"] "\n" [:option {:value "295"} "1956"] "\n" [:option {:value "309"} "1964"] "\n" [:option {:value "323"} "1968"] "\n" [:option {:value "333"} "1972"] "\n" [:option {:value "347"} "1976"] "\n" [:option {:value "361"} "1980"] "\n" [:option {:value "375"} "1984"] "\n" [:option {:value "389"} "1988"] "\n" [:option {:value "403"} "1992"] "\n" [:option {:value "417"} "1994"] "\n" [:option {:value "431"} "1998"] "\n" [:option {:value "443"} "2002"] "\n" [:option {:value "460"} "2006"] "\n" [:option {:value "924240"} "2010"] "\n" [:option {:value "350033"} "2014"] "\n" [:option {:value "9000240"} "2018"] "\n" [:option {:value "19019650"} "2022"] "\n" [:option {:value "15000080"} "2026"]] [:script {} "$('#other_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#other_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:a {:href "/event_names/140"} "Event type"]] [:h1 {:class "event_title"} "Two, Men" [:small {} [:a {:class "footnote", :href "#", :title "Originally scheduled for 11-12 February but start postponed after the four-man had to be postponed three days because of weather conditions.", :data-toggle "tooltip", :data-placement "right"} "1"]]] [:table {:class "biodata"} [:tbody {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Date"] [:td {} "14 – 15 February 1936"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Olympic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/39"} "Olympia-Bobbahn, Garmisch-Partenkirchen"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/253"} "46 from 13 countries"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Format"] [:td {:colspan "2"} "Four runs, total time determined placement."]] [:tr {} [:th {:valign "top"} "Details"] [:td {} "Curves: 17" [:br {}] "Length: 1525 m" [:br {}] "Start Altitude: 919 m" [:br {}] "Vertical Drop: 129 m"]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "The competition in the two-man event was wide open. There was defending World Champion " [:a {:href "/athletes/84588"} "Reto Capadrutt"] " of Switzerland, and home favourite " [:a {:href "/athletes/87930"} "Hanns Kilian"] " of Garmisch. The Romanians entered 1934 World Champion " [:a {:href "/athletes/85857"} "Alexandru Frim"] ", and Britain sent " [:a {:href "/results/260"} "four-man"] " bronze medalist " [:a {:href "/athletes/95307"} "Freddie McEvoy"] ". But none of these crews would medal."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The 1935 North American Championships were rather unknown in Europe, but that did not mean they weren’t strong. " [:a {:href "/athletes/84402"} "Ivan Brown"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/98830"} "Al Washbond"] " basically decided the competition competition in the very first run, taking an insurmountable lead of nearly three seconds. They did not win any of the remaining runs, but still had a rather comfortable 1.35 second lead over Switzerland II. That sled was steered by " [:a {:href "/athletes/85659"} "Fritz Feierabend"] ", who had already won a silver medal in the four-man event as a crewman for Capadrutt. He had placed 6th in the first run, but won the three remaining runs to move up to the silver medal position. Third place was taken by the second USA sled, which was steered by " [:a {:href "/athletes/84823"} "Gil Colgate, Jr."] " He was the great-grandson of William Colgate, founder of the soap and toothpaste company Colgate (now Colgate-Palmolive). He would later become a director of that corporation."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Further back in the field, " [:a {:href "/athletes/98711"} "Eduard, Baron von Falz-Fein"] " was one of the first four competitors from the tiny nation of Liechtenstein to compete in the Olympics. He had founded the Liechtenstein NOC the previous year to make participation possible. The Baron would return to the Olympics no less than 15 times, in various official functions, including for the Liechtensteinstein NOC, the Liechtenstein Cycling Association, and the " [:a {:href "/organizations/131"} "International Luge Federation"] "."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Pair"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Time"] [:th {} "Run #1"] [:th {} "Run #2"] [:th {} "Run #3"] [:th {} "Run #4"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/84402"} "Ivan Brown"] " / " [:a {:href "/athletes/98830"} "Al Washbond"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "5:29.29"] [:td {} "1:22.50 (1)"] [:td {} "1:21.02 (2)"] [:td {} "1:25.39 (3)"] [:td {} "1:20.38 (2)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/85659"} "Fritz Feierabend"] " / " [:a {:href "/athletes/83957"} "Joseph Beerli"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/SUI"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/SUI.png"}] "SUI"]] [:td {} "5:30.64"] [:td {} "1:26.34 (6)"] [:td {} "1:20.31 (1)"] [:td {} "1:24.11 (1)"] [:td {} "1:19.88 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/84823"} "Gil Colgate, Jr."] " / " [:a {:href "/athletes/89472"} "Dick Lawrence"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "5:33.96"] [:td {} "1:25.06 (2)"] [:td {} "1:21.94 (3)"] [:td {} "1:24.80 (2)"] [:td {} "1:22.16 (3)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Bronze"} "Bronze"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "4"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/95307